# Rakdos, the Muscle: "Whenever you sacrifice another creature, exile cards equal to its mana value from the top of target player's
# library. Until your next end step, you may play those cards, and mana of any type can be spent to cast those spells" and
# "Sacrifice another creature: Rakdos gains indestructible until end of turn. Tap it. Activate only once each turn" (CR 701.21a, 609.4b).
# Turn 3 Rakdos sacrifices Grizzly Bears (mana value 2): the top two cards of Bot2's library, an Island and a Lightning Bolt, are
# exiled; Rakdos is tapped and indestructible, and a second activation is refused (once each turn) with Memnite still there. Bot1
# plays the Island as its land drop and casts the Bolt with a Mox Jet's {B} (any type) for 3 damage (Bot2 on 17). Turn 5 a sacrificed
# Black Lotus (no creature) triggers nothing, and Memnite (mana value 0) exiles nothing. Turn 6 Bot2's Diabolic Edict makes Bot1
# sacrifice Rakdos itself, the only creature left: it is no "another creature", so nothing is exiled from Bot2's library.

